.Dd October 17, 2026
.Dt PATINA-SESSION 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm patina-session
.Nd the Patina desktop's login session
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Ar compositor-argument ...
.Nm
.Fl h | V
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is what the login screen runs for the Patina desktop.
It runs
.Xr patina-compositor 1
with the arguments given, and starts it again when it asks to restart or
when it crashes, so neither means logging in again.
The login screen's entry runs it as
.Ql patina-session --session .
.Pp
The compositor is found beside
.Nm ,
as
.Ql make install
puts them, or else on
.Ev PATH .
What happens when it exits depends on how:
.Bl -tag -width "anything else"
.It 0
It quit
.Pq Sy Ctrl+Alt+Backspace :
the session ends.
.It 75
It asked to restart
.Pq Sy Ctrl+Alt+Shift+Backspace , No or Restart Desktop in Xr patina-settings 1 :
it is started again at once.
Every window has closed; the desktop comes back.
.It anything else
It crashed: it is started again a second later.
Three crashes within a minute end the session instead, rather than a
loop the login screen never comes back from.
.El
.Pp
SIGTERM, SIGHUP and SIGINT, as the login manager sends when the session
ends, are passed on to the compositor, and
.Nm
exits once it has.
.Pp
While the screen is locked, the compositor keeps a marker in
.Ev XDG_RUNTIME_DIR ;
a compositor started again after a crash finds it and starts locked, so a
crash never opens the desktop.
.Nm
removes the marker when the session ends.
.Sh OPTIONS
Any argument but these is passed to the compositor.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl h , -help
Print a short usage message.
.It Fl V , -version
Print the version.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev PATINA_SESSION
Set for the compositor to this process's ID, so it knows a restart won't
end the session.
.It Ev XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
Where the lock marker,
.Pa patina-session- Ns Ar pid Ns Pa .locked ,
is kept.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 when the compositor quits or the session is told to end; 1 when the
compositor can't be started or crashed three times within a minute.
.Sh EXAMPLES
To end a session whose screen is stuck, from a text console:
.Pp
.Dl $ pkill patina-session
.Pp
Killing only the compositor counts as a crash, and restarts the desktop.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr patina-compositor 1 ,
.Xr patina-desktop 7
